      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-100129",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=2t+2,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t-2,\\,{p}_{3}(t)=t+1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{1}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $1$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(2)q(2),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\n- ${p}_{1}(t)\u22a5{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- ${p}_{2}(t)\u22a5\u0338{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n- $S={{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product"
