      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-104735",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the following set of polynomials:\n\n$$\n{p}_{1}(t)=3t,\\,{p}_{2}(t)=t+1,\\,{p}_{3}(t)={t}^{2}-1.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inner product in the vector space ${R}_{2}[t]$ of polynomials of degree at most $2$ in the variable $t$ is defined as \n\n$$\n\u27e8p(t),q(t)\u27e9=p(-1)q(-1)+p(0)q(0)+p(1)q(1),\n$$\n\nwhich of the following statements are true?\n\nI. ${p}_{1}(t)\u22a5\u0338{p}_{2}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nII. ${p}_{1}(t)\u22a5{p}_{3}(t)$ with respect to the given inner product\n\nIII. $S=\\{{p}_{1}(t),{p}_{2}(t),{p}_{3}(t)\\}$ is an orthogonal set with respect to the given inner product"
